{
	"version": 5,
	"id": "BXVwIS29m3vgaJjbp",
	"notes": "A Sicarian Ruststalker: a melee-specialist Skitarii variant built around raw speed and chordclaw/transonic blade work rather than firepower, fielded to close distance fast and shred whatever's waiting at the other end. Point math: ST 12 (+20), DX 15 (+100), IQ 9 (-20), HT 12 (+20) = 120; advantages +77 (Combat Reflexes 15 + Auto-senses, Skitarii Pattern 14 + Augmetic Legs, Combat Pattern 20 + Respirator Plugs 5 + Subdermal Armour Plating 5 + Enhanced Parry, All Parries 10 + Noospheric Link 8); disadvantages -72; skills +49. Total 174 points, in the same between-tiers band as the Skitarii Ranger/Vanguard, with the points shifted hard from IQ into DX to match a Ruststalker's role. Enable the disabled \"Sicarian Infiltrator Conversion\" lens below to reflavor this template as an Infiltrator instead (see that lens for what it changes). Weapons (chordclawss, transonic blades, flechette blasters, etc.) are equipment, not covered here.\n",
	"traits": [
		{
			"id": "tueRYulJ5JTeuedUV",
			"name": "ST",
			"local_notes": "Lore: Skitarii physical conditioning and augmetic reinforcement, as with any Skitarii pattern.\n\nDesign: ST 12 (+2), 10 pts/level (B15).",
			"tags": [
				"Attribute"
			],
			"base_points": 20,
			"features": [
				{
					"type": "attribute_bonus",
					"attribute": "st",
					"amount": 2
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"id": "tzyfC5EkMnwUp1lnW",
			"name": "DX",
			"local_notes": "Lore: Sicarian conditioning and cortex replacement prioritize reflex and blade-work above everything else, at real cost to the higher reasoning a Ranger or Vanguard keeps.\n\nDesign: DX 15 (+5), 20 pts/level (B15).",
			"tags": [
				"Attribute"
			],
			"base_points": 100,
			"features": [
				{
					"type": "attribute_bonus",
					"attribute": "dx",
					"amount": 5
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"id": "trdnbnmKg9mF0yqTW",
			"name": "IQ",
			"local_notes": "Lore: Codex background consistently describes Sicarian patterns as having sacrificed still more of their humanity and independent judgement than an already-conditioned Ranger or Vanguard.\n\nDesign: IQ 9 (-1), 20 pts/level (B15).",
			"tags": [
				"Attribute"
			],
			"base_points": -20,
			"features": [
				{
					"type": "attribute_bonus",
					"attribute": "iq",
					"amount": -1
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"id": "tJEbZXmsDO-2XB4C9",
			"name": "HT",
			"local_notes": "Lore: Augmetic reinforcement and conditioning produce real battlefield endurance.\n\nDesign: HT 12 (+2), 10 pts/level (B14).",
			"tags": [
				"Attribute"
			],
			"base_points": 20,
			"features": [
				{
					"type": "attribute_bonus",
					"attribute": "ht",
					"amount": 2
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"id": "tiboMk2F6n5MxeeT8",
			"name": "Combat Reflexes",
			"reference": "B43",
			"local_notes": "Lore: Drilled, doctrina-reinforced reactions under fire.\n\nDesign: Basic Set Combat Reflexes (B43), 15 points.",
			"tags": [
				"Advantage",
				"Mental",
				"Imperium"
			],
			"base_points": 15
		},
		{
			"id": "tY-LQp9GQuQuzzVqx",
			"name": "Auto-senses, Skitarii Pattern",
			"reference": "B60",
			"local_notes": "Infravision; Acute Vision +2.\n\nLore: The standard-issue ocular augmetic fitted to almost every Skitarii and forge-world menial: crude compared to a Magos' oculars, but enough to fight in smoke, dust, and near-total darkness without a lumen pack.\n\nDesign: Infravision (B60, 10) + Acute Vision +2 (B35, 2/level, 4) = 14 points.",
			"tags": [
				"Advantage",
				"Physical",
				"Imperium",
				"Adeptus Mechanicus"
			],
			"base_points": 14
		},
		{
			"id": "tphHSfojuAy4XYw6q",
			"name": "Augmetic Legs, Combat Pattern (Matched Pair)",
			"reference": "B46",
			"local_notes": "DR 6 on both legs; Basic Move +1 from servo-assisted stride.\n\nLore: Skitarii Rangers and Vanguard are routinely fielded with both legs replaced outright rather than one at a time; the matched pair's synchronized actuators give a longer, steadier stride than a single prosthetic bolted onto an otherwise natural gait.\n\nDesign: DR 6, Partial (both legs, a larger fraction of the body than a single limb) -50% (6x5=30, x0.5=15) + Basic Move +1 (B17, 5 points/level) = 20 points. Buying only one leg from this pair does not grant the Move bonus; use Augmetic Leg, Menial Pattern for a single prosthetic instead.",
			"tags": [
				"Advantage",
				"Physical",
				"Imperium",
				"Adeptus Mechanicus",
				"Skitarii"
			],
			"base_points": 20
		},
		{
			"id": "tvlIaYA8EzqPR-EfS",
			"name": "Respirator Plugs (Filtration Lungs)",
			"reference": "B55",
			"local_notes": "Lore: Grille-covered intake valves set into the throat or chest, scrubbing forge smog, promethium fumes, and toxic industrial atmosphere before it reaches the lungs — near-universal among Mechanicus adepts who spend their working lives on a forge-world's surface.\n\nDesign: Basic Set Filter Lungs (B55), 5 points.",
			"tags": [
				"Advantage",
				"Physical",
				"Imperium",
				"Adeptus Mechanicus"
			],
			"base_points": 5
		},
		{
			"id": "tzV5w6YuOrFA70Ldz",
			"name": "Subdermal Armour Plating",
			"reference": "B46",
			"local_notes": "DR, all locations; stacks with worn armor.\n\nLore: Ceramite or plasteel weave grafted beneath the skin across the whole body, rather than replacing a specific organ or limb — the augmetic equivalent of the Astartes' Ossmodula, bought by Tech-Priests who expect to take a hit.\n\nDesign: Plain Damage Resistance (B46), 5 points/level, no location restriction since it covers the whole body. Bought here at a default 2 levels (DR 10, 10 points); raise or lower the level to taste.",
			"tags": [
				"Advantage",
				"Physical",
				"Imperium",
				"Adeptus Mechanicus"
			],
			"points_per_level": 5,
			"can_level": true,
			"levels": 1
		},
		{
			"id": "t-MGtKBvmsrAqht0e",
			"name": "Enhanced Parry (All Parries)",
			"reference": "B51",
			"local_notes": "Lore: A Ruststalker's chordclaws and transonic blades are built for a whirling, evasive dueling style rather than a single locked-in stance; the pattern's conditioning and reflex augmetics make it unnervingly hard to land a solid counter-hit on one.\n\nDesign: Basic Set Enhanced Parry, All Parries (B51), 10 points.",
			"tags": [
				"Advantage",
				"Physical",
				"Imperium",
				"Adeptus Mechanicus"
			],
			"base_points": 10
		},
		{
			"id": "tpThJxgJgPmVKAF__",
			"name": "Noospheric Link",
			"reference": "B91",
			"local_notes": "Short-to-medium range wireless data-link to the Cult Mechanicus' noosphere: other Noospheric Link-bearing adepts and compatible cogitators/machine spirits only.\n\nLore: A subcutaneous vox-and-data transceiver that lets a Tech-Priest read and post to the layered, half-mystical data-cloud the Mechanicus calls the noosphere — status runes, binharic liturgy, and tactical chatter overlaid on the world for anyone plugged in, and gibberish static to anyone who isn't.\n\nDesign: Basic Set Telecommunication (Radio type, B91, 10 points) with the Racial limitation (B91, -20%, restricted to others who share the trait — here, other noosphere-linked adepts and machine spirits): 10 x 0.8 = 8 points. Pairs with the Language (Binharic) skill (Adeptus Mechanicus/Skills/Mechanicus Skills.skl) for the liturgical cant spoken over the link; the link itself is the hardware, the language is the learned code riding on it.",
			"tags": [
				"Advantage",
				"Mental",
				"Imperium",
				"Adeptus Mechanicus"
			],
			"base_points": 8
		},
		{
			"id": "Tl8wOGb82zY3Z-Yrl",
			"name": "Skitarii Conditioning",
			"local_notes": "Lore: Skitarii undergo extensive neural conditioning and cybernetic replacement of their own that, while far short of a Servitor's total lobotomy, strips away most of the emotional affect and small-talk that would otherwise mark them as still fully human — codex and Black Library background alike describe them as unnervingly flat and literal even next to other Mechanicus adepts.\n\nDesign: Low Empathy (B142, -20) + No Sense of Humor (B146, -10) + a 1-point Quirk (B9) for clipped, ritualized speech patterns = -31 points. Deliberately short of Servitor Lobotomy (Neural Excision) above: Skitarii still hold rank, opinions, and (per some Codex background) occasional flickers of the person they were, where a Servitor has none of that left.",
			"tags": [
				"Disadvantage",
				"Mental",
				"Imperium",
				"Adeptus Mechanicus",
				"Skitarii"
			],
			"container_type": "meta_trait",
			"children": [
				{
					"id": "tIu1to5RpkAuQMxKE",
					"name": "Low Empathy",
					"reference": "B142",
					"base_points": -20
				},
				{
					"id": "tuImJKagubVccYfUl",
					"name": "No Sense of Humor",
					"reference": "B146",
					"base_points": -10
				},
				{
					"id": "tEj0px16vZCVJW35L",
					"name": "Speaks Only in Clipped Binharic-Inflected Report",
					"tags": [
						"Quirk"
					],
					"base_points": -1
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"id": "tq630PEOZXA6iyQO6",
			"name": "Fanaticism (The Omnissiah)",
			"reference": "B136",
			"local_notes": "Lore: Doctrinal certainty that the Machine God — the same Emperor, in the Cult Mechanicus' own theology, understood as a being of pure technological perfection — must be served without question, and that His will (as interpreted by the Priesthood's hierarchy) justifies whatever it demands. Distinct from the Imperial Creed's Fanaticism (The God-Emperor) in Imperium/Traits/Imperial Traits.adq: the same shape of belief, aimed at a different reading of the same divinity.\n\nDesign: Basic Set Fanaticism (B136), flat -15, as the existing Imperial Fanaticism entry is built.",
			"tags": [
				"Disadvantage",
				"Mental",
				"Imperium",
				"Adeptus Mechanicus"
			],
			"base_points": -15
		},
		{
			"id": "tjBwSWlVYyxBuUdwX",
			"name": "Duty (Adeptus Mechanicus)",
			"reference": "B133",
			"local_notes": "Overridden to -15 (almost always hazardous): Sicarian service is combat service.\n\nLore: A sworn Tech-Priest, Enginseer, or Skitarii answers first to their Forge World and its Fabricator-General, not to any Guard officer or Administratum functionary they happen to be attached to — a binding, frequent, but not universally life-threatening obligation (unlike a Guardsman's), since a Mechanicus posting is at least as often archival or industrial as it is a battlefield one.\n\nDesign: Basic Set Duty (B133), fairly frequent but not \"almost always hazardous\" the way Duty (Astra Militarum) is (Imperium/Traits/ Imperial Traits.adq) — pegged one tier below that entry, at -10, to reflect the Priesthood's broader range of postings. A Skitarii or a field-attached Enginseer/Techmarine should reasonably use -15 instead; -10 is this template's baseline for a workshop- or forge-based adept.",
			"tags": [
				"Disadvantage",
				"Social",
				"Imperium",
				"Adeptus Mechanicus"
			],
			"base_points": -15
		},
		{
			"id": "tIify-6_AgloecIyD",
			"name": "Intolerance (Xenos)",
			"reference": "B140",
			"local_notes": "Lore: \"The alien is the enemy\" as baseline Imperial doctrine — not personal bigotry but state religion. Universal across Black Library fiction; only a minority of xenos-sympathetic characters (some Rogue Traders, Ordo Xenos radicals) lack it.\n\nDesign: Basic Set Intolerance (B140). Costed at -10, the \"very broad category\" end of the range the book allows, since \"all non-human sapient species\" is about as broad a target as Intolerance can name.",
			"tags": [
				"Disadvantage",
				"Mental",
				"Imperium"
			],
			"base_points": -10
		},
		{
			"id": "t1ldFm-2QXBv34ZtM",
			"name": "Even a Skitarii Finds Them Unsettling",
			"local_notes": "Lore: Codex and Black Library background both single out Sicarian patterns as disquieting even to their fellow Skitarii.\n\nDesign: Quirk (B9), roleplaying flag only.",
			"tags": [
				"Quirk",
				"Imperium"
			],
			"base_points": -1
		},
		{
			"id": "TVcm21e0F5Cm1VLFt",
			"name": "Lens: Sicarian Infiltrator Conversion",
			"local_notes": "Lore: Sicarian Infiltrators trade the Ruststalker's close-in chordclaw assault role for ranged ambush work with flechette blasters and taser goads: less pure melee speed, more patience and fieldcraft. Enabling this lens is a flag for that choice; rebalance the skill list by hand (shift points from Broadsword into Guns (Rifle) and Stealth) to match — this lens itself only carries the flavor perks that don't depend on the specific weapon loadout.\n\nDesign: Net 0 points, per-pattern flavor lens (see framework.md, origin lenses, for the pattern this follows).",
			"tags": [
				"Imperium",
				"Adeptus Mechanicus",
				"Skitarii"
			],
			"children": [
				{
					"id": "tWWXWdYyqrVqdw5dr",
					"name": "Ambush Discipline",
					"local_notes": "Lore: Infiltrators are drilled to hold a covered firing position rather than close to blade range.\n\nDesign: Perk (B9), +1 to Stealth.",
					"tags": [
						"Perk",
						"Imperium"
					],
					"base_points": 1,
					"features": [
						{
							"type": "skill_bonus",
							"selection_type": "skills_with_name",
							"name": {
								"compare": "is",
								"qualifier": "Stealth"
							},
							"amount": 1
						}
					]
				},
				{
					"id": "tmEefnlIMktZJeHsa",
					"name": "Prefers the Kill at Range",
					"local_notes": "Lore: An Infiltrator's conditioning steers it away from melee engagement whenever a shot is available instead.\n\nDesign: Quirk (B9), roleplaying flag only.",
					"tags": [
						"Quirk",
						"Imperium"
					],
					"base_points": -1
				}
			],
			"disabled": true
		}
	],
	"skills": [
		{
			"id": "sTdXYaVDCn27bHoQF",
			"name": "Broadsword",
			"local_notes": "Lore: Chordclaws and transonic blades are disruption-field-adjacent melee weapons per framework.md's weapon-skill table (Broadsword covers power/disruption-field blades generally).\n\nDesign: DX+5 (20) for 20 points, Average (B170).",
			"tags": [
				"Imperium",
				"Adeptus Mechanicus",
				"Skitarii"
			],
			"difficulty": "dx/a",
			"points": 20
		},
		{
			"id": "snerIfTSGsQp5DuSq",
			"name": "Acrobatics",
			"local_notes": "Lore: The evasive, leaping fighting style Ruststalkers are consistently depicted using.\n\nDesign: DX+0 (15) for 8 points, Hard.",
			"tags": [
				"Imperium"
			],
			"difficulty": "dx/h",
			"points": 8
		},
		{
			"id": "sGqr-A73mvkpU-aD_",
			"name": "Stealth",
			"local_notes": "Lore: Closing to blade range without being cut down first.\n\nDesign: DX+2 (17) for 8 points, Average.",
			"tags": [
				"Imperium"
			],
			"difficulty": "dx/a",
			"points": 8
		},
		{
			"id": "sM65O24PAODUJXQ16",
			"name": "Climbing",
			"local_notes": "Lore: Scaling obstacles to flank a target.\n\nDesign: DX+0 (15) for 2 points, Average.",
			"tags": [
				"Imperium"
			],
			"difficulty": "dx/a",
			"points": 2
		},
		{
			"id": "semSf3L3TZIdx7Ssh",
			"name": "Jumping",
			"local_notes": "Lore: Closing distance fast.\n\nDesign: DX+1 (16) for 2 points, Easy.",
			"tags": [
				"Imperium"
			],
			"difficulty": "dx/e",
			"points": 2
		},
		{
			"id": "sSiM5EynujSTxn5bM",
			"name": "Brawling",
			"local_notes": "Lore: Unarmed back-up when a blade is knocked away.\n\nDesign: DX+0 (15) for 1 point, Easy.",
			"tags": [
				"Imperium"
			],
			"difficulty": "dx/e",
			"points": 1
		},
		{
			"id": "sTLudbMTkpZZ45guL",
			"name": "Camouflage",
			"local_notes": "Lore: Basic concealment discipline.\n\nDesign: IQ+0 (9) for 1 point, Easy.",
			"tags": [
				"Imperium"
			],
			"difficulty": "iq/e",
			"points": 1
		},
		{
			"id": "smU5ZyxsqNipMtu6V",
			"name": "Tactics",
			"local_notes": "Lore: Enough small-unit tactics to coordinate a flanking rush.\n\nDesign: IQ-1 (8) for 2 points, Hard.",
			"tags": [
				"Imperium"
			],
			"difficulty": "iq/h",
			"points": 2
		},
		{
			"id": "sm-AzU2_Al95HwNMI",
			"name": "Theology",
			"local_notes": "Lore: A Sicarian's much-reduced grasp of doctrine, retained more as ritual than understanding; see Imperium/Skills/Imperial Skills.skl.\n\nDesign: IQ-2 (7) for 2 points, Hard.",
			"tags": [
				"Imperium",
				"Adeptus Mechanicus"
			],
			"specialization": "Cult Mechanicus",
			"difficulty": "iq/h",
			"points": 2
		},
		{
			"id": "savPHBkt28dDhStro",
			"name": "Savoir-Faire",
			"reference": "B218",
			"local_notes": "Lore: Court protocol inside the Priesthood: correct forms of address for a Magos or Archmagos, ritual precedence between Forge Worlds and Explorator fleets, and which questions are simply never asked of a superior adept. Not attested under this exact name in the fiction, but the Mechanicus is consistently shown (across Black Library and codex background) to run on a court culture at least as rigid as the Ecclesiarchy's own.\n\nDesign: IQ+0 (9) for 1 point, Easy.",
			"tags": [
				"Mental",
				"Imperium",
				"Adeptus Mechanicus"
			],
			"specialization": "Adeptus Mechanicus",
			"difficulty": "iq/e",
			"defaults": [
				{
					"type": "iq",
					"modifier": -4
				}
			],
			"points": 1
		},
		{
			"id": "skjqKw0AxlqwPVKRQ",
			"name": "Intimidation",
			"local_notes": "Lore: A rushing, augmetic-clawed Ruststalker is intimidating before it even reaches you.\n\nDesign: Will+0 (9) for 2 points, Average.",
			"tags": [
				"Imperium"
			],
			"difficulty": "will/a",
			"points": 2
		}
	],
	"equipment": []
